#=GF RA   Warner KD, Homan P, Weeks KM, Smith AG, Abell C, Ferre-D'Amare AR
#=GF RL   Chem Biol. 2014;21:591-595.
#=GF CC   Vitamin B(1) in its active form thiamin pyrophosphate (TPP) is an
#=GF CC   essential coenzyme that is synthesised by coupling of pyrimidine and
#=GF CC   thiazole moieties in bacteria. The previously detected thiamin-regulatory
#=GF CC   element, thi box [1] was extended, resulting in a new, highly conserved
#=GF CC   RNA secondary structure, the THI element, which is widely distributed in
#=GF CC   eubacteria and also occurs in some archaea. Analysis of operon structures
#=GF CC   identified a large number of new candidate thiamin-regulated genes, mostly
#=GF CC   transporters, in various prokaryotic organisms [2]. The THI element is a
#=GF CC   riboswitch [3] that directly binds to TPP to regulate gene expression
#=GF CC   through a variety of mechanisms in archaea, bacteria and eukaryotes [4,5].
#=GF CC   through a variety of mechanisms in archaea, bacteria and eukaryotes [4,5].
#=GF CC   Tandem TPP riboswitches have been reported [6] where both TPP riboswitches
#=GF CC   respond independently to TPP. The structure of TPP riboswitch has been
#=GF CC   reported for Escherichia coli and Arabidopsis thaliana [7-12].
#=GF WK   TPP_riboswitch
#=GF SQ   115

